strip_ckpt.py against Team 7's export_safetensors(), on a commit with dry run 2's parameter split (#869:
176,398,881 parameters, 165,740,544 with one optimizer buffer each), saved by Team 7's Checkpointer; --scale 2 doubles
every tensor count (352,797,762 parameters).

Where: Linux (Docker python:3.11-slim on a 4-CPU, 16 GB VM on an Apple M4 Pro), torch 2.15.0+cpu, 4 threads. The commit
is read right after it is written, so the page cache is warm: the times are CPU and memory times, and "Read" counts
bytes through read() (rchar), from the cache or the disk. On a network store the read bytes set the time.
The probe bits are saved for a GPU device class ('cuda:NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3'), as in a GPU-trained run: the export
runs the CPU probe but cannot compare it. One SGD-momentum optimizer keeps one buffer per parameter, so the commit is
about 3% smaller than dry run 2's would be (no second AdamW buffer on 10.7M parameters). The tensor count (192 at
scale 1) is not the run's. For --verify fingerprints the build adds MANIFEST.json fingerprints of the model.* tensors,
made with Team 7's own fingerprints(), as Team 7's save would keep them (a proposal: state_digest() computes them
already). Each path runs in a fresh process.

Command:
  python teams/09-evaluation/harness_lab/tests/bench_strip.py --work /tmp/d1 --scale 1    (and --scale 2)
  ... --strip <the strip before streaming, commit 861e2b7e>, and --group-mb 256 / 64, for the comparisons below

Checks in the same state: harness_lab/tests on Linux, 95 passed, 3 runs (test_strip_ckpt.py: 19, one of them on a
commit saved by FSDP2 over 2 ranks). The real Team 5 model check is in check_strip_team5.log.

== 1. The final strip (streaming, default --group-mb 256) against the export
